                     <title>Iob glo. (frgm., 3 leaves)</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Perhaps from no. 173 in the Inventory (C),
                        1501, of Canterbury College, Oxford, which was still there in 1534; see
                        Pantin, Cant. Coll., OHS N.S. 6, (1946) 23, 117.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">B 47 used as pastedowns in St John's College,
                        Oxford, O.2.26 (Petrus Lombardus, Sententiae, Louvain, 1546), rebound, s.
                        xix.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Given by Henry Cole, 'precium iiij s' 1548' in
                        Cole's hand.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">C. de Hamel, Sotheby cat., 14 Dec. 1977, lot
                        48, suggested that the pastedowns in Bamburgh Sel. 40 (Oxford binding) are
                        also from this MS.</note>
